  8→{"type":"consensus","id":"C8","text":"Within EGPT's information-theoretic framework, the argument is internally coherent.","source":"both","exchange":12,"date":"2026-03-13"}
  9→{"type":"consensus","id":"C9","text":"The von Neumann–Gödel 1931 parallel is the correct frame for the core disagreement.","source":"both","exchange":12,"date":"2026-03-13"}
 10→{"type":"consensus","id":"C10","text":"The gap has been compressed to one identifiable point: RECT applied to decision problems.","source":"both","exchange":12,"date":"2026-03-13"}
 11→{"type":"consensus","id":"C11","text":"Shannon coding is stronger than bijection. Denumerable.eqv is the weaker tool.","source":"both","exchange":8,"date":"2026-03-13"}
 12→{"type":"consensus","id":"C12","text":"computeTableau? exists and handles both SAT and UNSAT. Not yet connected to time-complexity chain.","source":"both","exchange":13,"date":"2026-03-13"}
 13→{"type":"concession","id":"Y1","who":"skeptic","text":"The walk construction is a legitimate polynomial-time verifier (given a witness).","exchange":5,"date":"2026-03-13"}
 14→{"type":"concession","id":"Y2","who":"skeptic","text":"EGPT's framework is not trivially wrong — it's a genuine alternative axiomatization.","exchange":8,"date":"2026-03-13"}
 15→{"type":"concession","id":"Y3","who":"skeptic","text":"The zero-probability event argument via IsEntropyZeroInvariance is sharper than initially appreciated.","exchange":13,"date":"2026-03-13"}
 16→{"type":"concession","id":"Y4","who":"skeptic","text":"The gap is structural (definitional), not instantial (no counterexample exists).","exchange":12,"date":"2026-03-13"}
 17→{"type":"concession","id":"Y5","who":"advocate","text":"P_info uses ∃ endpoint which requires a satisfying assignment to exist.","exchange":9,"date":"2026-03-13"}
 18→{"type":"concession","id":"Y6","who":"advocate","text":"equivSyntacticCNF_to_ParticlePath uses Denumerable.eqv, weaker than Shannon coding.","exchange":8,"date":"2026-03-13"}
 19→{"type":"concession","id":"Y7","who":"advocate","text":"Experimental code in Decomposition.lean is NOT part of the proof chain.","exchange":8,"date":"2026-03-13"}
 20→{"type":"concession","id":"Y8","who":"advocate","text":"The gap between P_info and standard P is real at the definitional level.","exchange":12,"date":"2026-03-13"}
