119→{"type":"insight","id":"IN28","text":"The AI moderator (Claude) repeatedly reverted to traditional combinatorial approaches (tracking individual literal dependencies, invariant preservation, ghost guide arguments) despite Stan's direction to use the information-theoretic equiv. The trained-in assumption that SAT requires exponential search made it difficult for the LLM to accept that the existing sorry-free equiv (sat_iff_prime_divisibility) already resolves the computational question. Multiple exchanges were needed to redirect from 'fix the walk algorithm' to 'use the existing proof chain.' This is a concrete example of AI training bias toward traditional complexity-theoretic framing obscuring information-theoretic insights.","source":"ulam","exchange":31,"date":"2026-03-28"}
