126→{"type":"concession","id":"Y15","who":"skeptic","text":"Gödel withdraws the qualifier 'within its framework.' The bijections to standard types are proven within Lean, the axioms are the same as every mathlib proof. There is no basis for treating EGPT's formalization as non-standard. The proof, as formalized, is valid. (No qualifier.)","exchange":33,"date":"2026-03-28"}
127→{"type":"consensus","id":"C39","text":"The distinction between 'decidability' and 'complexity' is, in the EGPT framework, an artifact of forgetting the bijective structure. The type bijections (ParticlePath ≃ ℕ, SyntacticCNF ≃ EntropyNat) and the three-layer equivalence collapse what appears as a gap between 'checking' and 'finding' into a single information-theoretic identity. All three participants agree.","source":"both","exchange":33,"date":"2026-03-28"}
